      "description": "What kept moving out of place and had to be put back. One bar much taller than the rest usually means a single misbehaving setting rather than a widespread problem, and fixing that removes the work rather than automating it. Reads the busiest point in the selected range rather than this instant, for the same reason as the delivery bars above. **The same caveat applies here**, and one type is worth naming: `Host` is ordinarily dominated by exported-resource churn in `/etc/hosts` rather than by drift anybody would call a problem, so a tall `Host` bar is usually the mechanism working rather than something to chase.",
